SSTP core attribution
=====================

The files under kittoku/osc are derived from kittoku's Open-SSTP-Client, an
MIT-licensed SSTP (Secure Socket Tunneling Protocol) client for Android:

    https://github.com/kittoku/Open-SSTP-Client
    Copyright (c) 2024 kittoku
    (the MIT license text ships alongside this file: LICENSE)

DeltaTor's use of it
--------------------

This tree is the vendored core, reduced to what a tunnel needs:

- no in-app settings are read: every checkpoint of the original client
  (SharedPreferences, the floating logger, the certificate picker, app-based
  routing rules) was replaced by kittoku/osc/SstpParams + SharedBridge, driven by
  DeltaTor's own configuration and owned by io.deltator.TorVpnService;
- the terminal was re-pointed: every connection is dialled as a raw SOCKS5
  client through Tor's local bridge (127.0.0.1, per Config.proxyPort) instead
  of the original HTTP CONNECT proxy support, so the whole chain is
  Tor-first;
- the pool it connects to is VPN Gate's public server hub, fetched, probed and
  ranked by io.deltator.ProxyChainManager, and driven by the Proxy Chain UI.

Behaviour covered by the code lives in the engine:
io.deltator.tunnel.SstpChainEngine.
